From: Mate Molnar <matemolnar88@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pvr: 4x region header and TPC headroom on simple parameter format v1 (experiment)

region_header_size stays the plain tile count (the firmware copies it
straight into ISP_RGN). The buffers get 4x headroom for the tile scale
experiment that investigates the half-per-axis coverage on the GE8300.
---
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
@@ -294,6 +294,10 @@
       size /= (2U * 2U);
    }
 
+   /* Version 1: same 4x headroom as the region headers (see above). */
+   if (version == 1)
+      size *= 4U;
+
    size *= ROGUE_TAIL_POINTER_SIZE;
 
    if (layers > 1) {
@@ -390,6 +394,13 @@
    rgn_headers_size *= num_tiles_y / group_size;
    rgn_headers_size *= single_rgn_header_size;
 
+   /* Version 1: headroom (4x) while the GE8300 tile coverage is being
+    * investigated; the kernel's brn tile_scale experiment needs it.
+    * ponytail: drop once the 1/2-per-axis coverage bug is understood.
+    */
+   if (version == 1)
+      rgn_headers_size *= 4U;
+
    if (PVR_HAS_FEATURE(dev_info, simple_internal_parameter_format)) {
       rgn_headers_size =
          ALIGN_POT(rgn_headers_size, ROGUE_CR_TE_PSGREGION_ADDR_BASE_ALIGNMENT);
